hadiths[14]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15412","Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from al-Rabi ibn Sabrah, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade mutah of women on the day of the conquest."
"15413","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ismail ibn Umayyah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, he said: We were discussing mutah, the mutah of women, at Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz, so al-Rabi ibn Sabrah said: I heard my father saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the farewell hajj forbidding mutah marriage."
"15414","Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn al-Rabi ibn Sabrah al-Juhani narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a boy reaches seven years, he is commanded to pray, and when he reaches ten, he is beaten for it."
"15415","Zayd narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn al-Rabi ibn Sabrah informed me, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you prays, let him screen himself for his prayer, even with an arrow."
"15416","Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn al-Rabi ibn Sabrah al-Juhani narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade praying in the resting places of camels, and permitted praying in the resting places of sheep."
"15417","Yaqub ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn al-Rabi ibn Sabrah narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The screen of a man in prayer is an arrow, and when one of you prays, let him screen himself with an arrow. He said: Yaqub narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn al-Rabi ibn Sabrah narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us to pray in the resting places of camels, and permitted us to pray in the resting places of sheep, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade mutah."
"15418","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from al-Rabi ibn Sabrah, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the mutah of women."
"15419","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Umar informed me, from al-Rabi ibn Sabrah, from his father, he said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from Madinah in the farewell hajj, until when we were at Usfan, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed the umrah has entered into the hajj. So Suraqah ibn Malik, or Malik ibn Suraqah, Abd al-Aziz doubted, said to him: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), teach us as teaching a people as if born today: Is this umrah of ours for this year of ours, or forever? He said: No, rather forever. So when we arrived at Makkah, we circumambulated the House and between al-Safa and al-Marwah, then he commanded us with the mutah of women. So we returned to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, they have refused except for a named term. He said: Then do it. He said: So I went out, I and a companion of mine; upon me was a cloak and upon him was a cloak. So we entered upon a woman and offered ourselves to her. So she kept looking at the cloak of my companion, seeing it better than my cloak, and looking at me, seeing me younger than him. So she said: A cloak for a cloak, and she chose me. So I married her for ten for my cloak, and I spent that night with her. So when morning came, I went early to the mosque, and I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while upon the minbar, preaching, saying: Whoever among you married a woman for a term, let him give her what he named for her, and let him not take back anything of what he gave her, and let him part from her, for indeed Allah, the Exalted, has forbidden it to you until the Day of Resurrection."
"15420","Affan narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, he said: Umarah ibn Ghazziyah al-Ansari narrated to us, he said: Al-Rabi ibn Sabrah al-Juhani narrated to us, from his father, he said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of the conquest, and we stayed fifteen days and nights. He said: He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted mutah. He said: And I went out, I and a cousin of mine, in the lower part of Makkah, or he said in the upper part of Makkah, and we met a young woman of Banu Amir ibn Sasah as if she were a tall young she-camel. He said: And I was close to plain-looking, and upon me was a new fresh cloak, and upon my cousin was a worn cloak. He said: So we said to her: Would you have one of us enjoy from you? She said: And is that proper? He said: We said: Yes. He said: So she kept looking at my cousin. So I said to her: This cloak of mine is new and fresh, and this cloak of my cousin is worn and threadbare. She said: This cloak of your cousin, there is no harm in it. He said: So he enjoyed from her. And we did not leave Makkah until the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade it."
"15421","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, he said: I heard Abd Rabbih ibn Said narrating, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz, from al-Rabi ibn Sabrah, from his father, who is called al-Sabri, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he commanded them with mutah. He said: So I and a man proposed to a woman. He said: So I met the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) after three, and he was forbidding it with the severest forbidding, and saying about it the severest speech, and prohibiting it with the severest prohibition."
"15422","Yaqub narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn al-Rabi ibn Sabrah narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade praying in the resting places of camels, and permitted praying in the resting places of sheep."
"15423","Yunus narrated to us, Layth, meaning Ibn Sad, narrated to us, he said: Al-Rabi ibn Sabrah narrated to me, from his father Sabrah al-Juhani, that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted us mutah. He said: So I set out, I and a man older than me of the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and we met a young woman of Banu Amir as if she were a young she-camel with a long neck. So we offered ourselves to her, and she said: What will you two offer? He said: Each one of us his cloak. He said: And the cloak of my companion was better than my cloak, and I was younger than him. She said: So she kept looking at the cloak of my companion, then she said: You and your cloak will suffice me. He said: So I stayed with her three. He said: Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever has with him any of the women he enjoyed, let him release her. He said: So I parted from her."
"15424","Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from al-Rabi ibn Sabrah, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade mutah marriage."
"15425","Waki narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, he said: Al-Rabi ibn Sabrah al-Juhani informed me, from his father, he said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and when we completed our umrah, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to us: Enjoy from these women. He said: And enjoyment with us that day meant marriage. He said: So we offered that to the women, and they refused except that a term be fixed between us and them. He said: So we mentioned that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: Do it. So I set out, I and a cousin of mine; with him was a cloak and with me was a cloak, and his cloak was better than my cloak, and I was younger than him. So we came to a woman and offered that to her. So my youth pleased her, and the cloak of my cousin pleased her. So she said: A cloak like a cloak. He said: So I married her, and the term between me and her was ten. He said: So I spent that night with her, then in the morning I went early to the mosque, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was between the door and the stone, preaching to the people, saying: O people, I had permitted you enjoyment from these women. Indeed Allah, the Blessed and Exalted, has forbidden that until the Day of Resurrection. So whoever has with him any of them, let him release her, and do not take anything of what you gave them."
